    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17434" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-ungo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, unctum, 3, v.
				a., <i>to anoint</i> (a Plautinian word): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eluas tu an exungare, ciccum non interduim,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 2, 7, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exunctum, elutum in balineis,</span>”
				<i>spent on ointments</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Trin. 2, 4, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
